window.docContents[224].resolve({"/Sub/#Type-Systems--Sub___-Subtyping--Formal-Definitions--Substitution":{"contents":"The definition of substitution remains exactly the same as for the\npure STLC.\n\ndef subst (x : String) (s : Tm) (t : Tm) : Tm :=\n  match t with\n  -- pure STLC\n  | .var y =>\n      if x = y then s else t\n  | .abs y τ t₁ =>\n      if x = y then t else <{ λ y : τ . [x := s] t₁ }>\n  | .app t₁ t₂ =>\n      <{ ([x := s] t₁) ([x := s] t₂) }>\n  -- unit\n  | .unit => <{ unit }>\n  -- bools\n  | .tru => <{ true }>\n  | .fls => <{ false }>\n  | .ite t₁ t₂ t₃ =>\n      <{ if [x := s] t₁ then [x := s] t₂ else [x := s] t₃ }>\n\n  -- Complete the following cases when you do the `products` exercise later\n  | .pair t₁ t₂ =>\n      sorry\n  | .fst t =>\n      sorry\n  | .snd t =>\n      sorry\n\n\nopen Lean PrettyPrinter in\n@[app_unexpander subst]\ndef unexpandSubst : Unexpander := StlcCommon.Delab.unexpandSubst\n\n\n","context":"Type Systems\u0009Sub: Subtyping\u0009Formal Definitions","header":"8.2.2. Substitution","id":"/Sub/#Type-Systems--Sub___-Subtyping--Formal-Definitions--Substitution"}});